From cd58a9defec2ed7e796079bc4b9358ec230687f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:09:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Wave 1, forms: every form speaks in plain words at the
 box

The owner asked (2026-11-11) for a stress test of every touch and input. This is the
form kit's share of wave 1, fixed once for every page: a wrong box gets its words under
it (no browser bubble), nothing moves under a finger, a refusal sits right above the
buttons, figures are read as typed ("1,200", "5%"), Return walks the boxes and saves
only from the last, a keyboard open puts the cursor in the first box, Cancel goes back
to the row, a row's form opens under its row (ui.openUnder), a one-tap change can be
undone (ui.undoable, ui.notice with Undo), an answer is brought into view (ui.reveal).
Optional boxes can fold under one quiet line, "More details (optional)" (more: true on
a field): shut by default, open by themselves for a saved value or a wrong box. No
page marks a field yet, so nothing on screen changes until a page asks.

New: core/ui/checks.js and core/ui/undo.js (pure, node-tested), tests/ui-checks.test.mjs,
tests/ui-undo.test.mjs, tests/ui-kit-helpers.test.mjs (ui.reveal, ui.spanOf,
ui.openUnder, ui.fieldError, ui.numberBox, ui.wordsFor on a stand-in screen);
tools/check.mjs keeps both pure. core/ui/base.css: the forms block after the form rules
and one reduced-motion line at the end. docs/CONVENTIONS.md: "Forms: asking, checking,
answering" and the input schema's new options. No page file changes.

Agent: claude-b

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
